            "text": "Our processes follow NIST SP 800-88 Rev. 2 guidelines for media sanitization and support HIPAA technical safeguards for protected health information at facilities such as Kern Medical and Adventist Health Bakersfield. We provide serialized certificates of destruction, complete chain of custody documentation, and accurate reporting suitable for regulatory audits under the California Electronic Waste Recycling Act and DTSC universal waste rules."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Where is equipment from Bakersfield processed?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Equipment collected in Bakersfield is staged locally and transported to one of our two certified processing facilities in Jacksonville, Texas and Houston, Texas where all data destruction and material recovery takes place. STS Electronic Recycling has served organizations across all 50 states since 2011 from our 200,000 sq ft processing operation with zero landfill commitment and full downstream tracking."
